## 18. Common Errors & Pitfalls

### N-Queens Mistakes

| Mistake | Symptom | Fix |
|---------|---------|-----|
| Wrong diagonal formula | Queens attack each other diagonally | Use `r-c` for primary, `r+c` for anti-diagonal |
| Not unmark after backtrack | Cells blocked incorrectly in sibling branches | Always remove from all 3 sets after recursion |
| Not copying board to result | All results show the same (empty) board | Add `boardToList(board)` — make a snapshot |
| Checking wrong direction | Missed attacks | Check col, both diagonals — that's all you need |
| Placing multiple queens per row | Invalid solutions | Fix: one recursive call per row, advance row by 1 |

### Sudoku Mistakes

| Mistake | Symptom | Fix |
|---------|---------|-----|
| Not resetting cell on backtrack | Board corrupted; wrong solution | `board[r][c] = '.'` after failed recursion |
| Box index formula wrong | Some box constraints missed | `boxIndex = (r/3)*3 + (c/3)` |
| Returning true prematurely | Stops before valid solution found | Only return `true` when `row == 9` |
| Forgetting to skip filled cells | Overwrites given digits | Check `if board[r][c] != '.'` first |
| Not propagating `true` upward | Correct solution found but discarded | `if (solve(...)) return true;` after placement |

